{"h":3396,"lines":[{"y":0.036339587010684293,"w":0.06301954269409181,"t":"Test 4","x":0.0879463429141389,"h":0.016636938313011274,"c":1},{"h":0.018895348053517669,"t":"READING","w":0.13374485015869142,"y":0.079941860699500822,"c":1,"x":0.44032922065110691},{"h":0.015998644317698929,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","c":1,"x":0.088477369927430327,"y":0.14389534868765441,"w":0.3086419677734375},{"w":0.8168724060058592,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","h":0.018915891928161677,"y":0.18021201464929759,"c":1,"x":0.088477377306360364},{"x":0.088095321849258001,"w":0.1714577611287435,"t":"Passage 1 below.","c":1,"y":0.19652106237277767,"h":0.021055019365182615},{"y":0.23546511608623344,"t":"Roman tunnels","x":0.39506173158378988,"w":0.22839505513509117,"h":0.020424165489816848,"c":1},{"t":"The Romans, who once controlled areas of Europe, North Africa and","y":0.27323186653449627,"w":0.76555501302083329,"x":0.12546354536138324,"h":0.02149080022625427,"c":1},{"y":0.28965961331143419,"c":1,"h":0.024708964658991084,"t":"Asia Minor, adopted the construction techniques of other civilizations to","w":0.7964805603027344,"x":0.10896882958342549},{"w":0.3395061747233073,"x":0.33744855978340799,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"y":0.30948174349768653,"t":"build tunnels in their territories"},{"w":0.80041152954101569,"y":0.34738372077042357,"c":1,"x":0.088477362733766829,"h":0.017457268403753057,"t":"The Persians, who lived in present-day Iran, were one of the first civilizations to build tunnels"},{"x":0.086352715774410449,"w":0.77791997273763025,"c":1,"t":"that provided a reliable supply of water to human settlements in dry areas. In the early first","y":0.36409889836861531,"h":0.018841590701621058},{"y":0.38129648289377882,"c":1,"h":0.020330361679670172,"x":0.086341472465827088,"w":0.79028564453125005,"t":"millennium BCE, they introduced the ganat method of tunnel construction, which consisted"},{"w":0.81079600016276043,"h":0.019922211538074386,"x":0.088421731703609799,"c":1,"t":"of placing posts over a hill in a straight line, to ensure that the tunnel kept to its route, and then","y":0.39957682664016825},{"t":"digging vertical shafts down into the ground at regular intervals. Underground, workers removed","y":0.41715117922750766,"c":1,"h":0.018993555165572773,"x":0.088414546286144008,"w":0.82524363199869788},{"t":"the earth from between the ends of the shafts, creating a tunnel. The excavated soil was taken up","x":0.086351256487565239,"y":0.43473850042864115,"w":0.82524978637695323,"h":0.020071692404954766,"c":1},{"h":0.019438315617322122,"c":1,"t":"to the surface using the shafts, which also provided ventilation during the work. Once the tunnel","x":0.086368377630208118,"w":0.82521916707356779,"y":0.45346796955888702},{"y":0.47085099061451796,"w":0.80877649943033858,"h":0.018673267746421085,"x":0.088412858851163775,"c":1,"t":"was completed, it allowed water to flow from the top of a hillside down towards a canal, which"},{"y":0.48969375738466492,"c":1,"x":0.088477374317206453,"h":0.017667844522968212,"w":0.83539093017578125,"t":"supplied water for human use. Remarkably, some ganats built by the Persians 2,700 years ago are"},{"t":"still in use today.","w":0.14923263549804688,"x":0.088020575767140535,"c":1,"h":0.019164636924213552,"y":0.50595808078069038},{"x":0.088477377795862247,"w":0.75925923665364581,"y":0.5421083629917941,"t":"They later passed on their knowledge to the Romans, who also used the ganat method to","h":0.016031172025610885,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.088368812233614924,"h":0.019845371673188561,"y":0.55863350600609707,"t":"construct water-supply tunnels for agriculture. Roman ganat tunnels were constructed with","w":0.7800569152832032},{"x":0.088419263206129792,"y":0.57681941306625462,"w":0.782009785970052,"h":0.018010354013970886,"c":1,"t":"vertical shafts dug at intervals of between 30 and 60 meters. The shafts were equipped with"},{"w":0.78405400594075525,"c":1,"h":0.01842119836975753,"t":"handholds and footholds to help those climbing in and out of them and were covered with a","x":0.088421081234825935,"y":0.59438288193697209},{"t":"wooden or stone lid. To ensure that the shafts were vertical, Romans hung a plumb line from a","y":0.61249261084384954,"h":0.019868293555521443,"x":0.088407414712262947,"c":1,"w":0.80672831217447916},{"c":1,"y":0.63010895215255436,"x":0.086358343690479844,"w":0.82317499796549476,"h":0.01871625722788528,"t":"rod placed across the top of each shaft and made sure that the weight at the end of it hung in the"},{"t":"center of the shaft. Plumb lines were also used to measure the depth of the shaft and to determine","y":0.6481947781775812,"w":0.83342859903971356,"h":0.017164949253113737,"c":1,"x":0.088426037123130449},{"y":0.66543257669693501,"x":0.0884247164178215,"t":"the slope of the tunnel. The 5.6-kilometer-long Claudius tunnel, built in 41 CE to drain the Fucine","h":0.018971008462535188,"w":0.83962285359700517,"c":1},{"t":"Lake in central Italy, had shafts that were up to 122 meters deep, took 11 years to build and","x":0.088477357368146742,"h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.68459302309661896,"w":0.77983540852864586,"c":1},{"t":"involved approximately 30,000 workers.","c":1,"y":0.70347467620137083,"x":0.08641975470027044,"w":0.34979423522949216,"h":0.017455556507807057},{"t":"By the 6th century BCE, a second method of tunnel construction appeared called the counter-","y":0.73613161791549442,"x":0.090461816467285225,"w":0.80466384887695308,"h":0.018826273501410751,"c":1},{"t":"excavation method, in which the tunnel was constructed from both ends. It was used to cut","x":0.08847737465457764,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"y":0.7558139533553504,"w":0.77777776082356775},{"x":0.088430946363866572,"y":0.77178163260534927,"t":"through high mountains when the ganat method was not a practical alternative. This method","w":0.79023203531901043,"h":0.018493616398428281,"c":1},{"t":"required greater planning and advanced knowledge of surveying, mathematics and geometry","y":0.79063604263524268,"w":0.79423868815104159,"h":0.017503492402524912,"c":1,"x":0.088477363632907785},{"y":0.80575733025602425,"t":"as both ends of a tunnel had to meet correctly at the center of the mountain. Adjustments to the","c":1,"w":0.81503397623697915,"h":0.021711807790156468,"x":0.088365406687620218},{"y":0.82558139517981599,"c":1,"h":0.017469252798666735,"x":0.090534990718452099,"w":0.81687240600585953,"t":"direction of the tunnel also had to be made whenever builders encountered geological problems"},{"c":1,"t":"or when it deviated from its set path. They constantly checked the tunnel's advancing direction,","x":0.09053497552228805,"w":0.81275721232096354,"h":0.017441860778592999,"y":0.84302325561929803},{"c":1,"y":0.90843023238112497,"t":"82","h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.090534978948152031,"w":0.02674897193908693},{"x":0.71947457881876942,"c":1,"y":0.95563152624206638,"w":0.2523199462890624,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.02837258373750251}],"w":2400}